1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,920
<i>- There's still time to withdraw.</i>
<i>- Yeah.</i>

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,840
<i>If you don't have a band,</i>
<i>you can't compete.</i>

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:07,600
<i>Do you think anyone will actually apply?</i>

4
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:10,080
If we can't find applicants ourselves,
we'll have to rely on the universe.

5
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,440
<i>"A moonlight-bathing ritual</i>
<i>to ward off bad luck."</i>

6
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,640
- You want me to get naked?
- I think you should try it.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,600
- How about this? You jump, I jump. Deal?
- Huh?

8
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:20,400
May the moonlight shining down tonight

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,280
cleanse Khobfa of every bit of bad luck.

10
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:27,000
And please let the person standing
in front of me become my boyfriend.

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,520
Hello, everyone.

12
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,080
Right now, our band
is looking for just three more members.

13
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:41,080
If you're interested in joining Horizon,
come meet us in the audition room.

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,080
<i>Anyone thinking of joining this band</i>
<i>should think twice.</i>

15
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,280
<i>The reason no one wants to join is that…</i>

16
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,120
<i>Never mind.</i>

17
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,600
<i>What made you even want</i>
<i>to enter a band competition?</i>

18
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,360
<i>Hang in there.</i>

19
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,680
<i>It must be exhausting to try this hard.</i>

20
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:59,160
If you can't say anything nice,
then don't say anything at all. Got it?

21
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:01,200
What the hell is wrong with you all?

22
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:03,440
- You--
- Hey, calm down. Don't insult them.

23
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:06,600
If you're interested in the audition,
see you later today.

24
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,200
- Damn!
- Relax.

25
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,320
You've got talent.

26
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,360
I want them to see it and shut up already.

27
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,920
Smile a little.

28
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,200
No one wants to join a band with someone
who's always frowning. Trust me.

29
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,720
What? Why did you come close?

30
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,520
Why isn't anyone coming?

31
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,280
I told you.

32
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:06,400
You look too grumpy.
No one wants to be in a band with you.

33
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:10,759
What?

34
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,840
Ohm! Jinnie!

35
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,600
Holy shit, it actually worked.

36
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,480
Friends don't abandon each other.

37
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:22,240
Come on, Rin, Khobfa.

38
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,680
Let's chase our dreams.

39
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:29,160
Hey, aren't we still one member short?

40
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,640
If Ohm and Jinnie are joining us,
then we only have one choice left.

41
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:41,560
THE GRANDEST CONTEST OF OUR UNIVERSITY

42
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,400
AUDITION REGISTRATION

43
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,560
Have Rin and Khobfa signed up yet?

44
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,800
Not yet.

45
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,600
- Maybe they couldn't find enough members.
- How do you know we couldn't?

46
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,320
You're one person short.

47
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:11,040
Rin.

48
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,640
You told him already, right?

49
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,399
Yeah, I did. He said yes.

50
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,600
Then why isn't he here yet?

51
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,360
Where's your last member?

52
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,480
I'm here.

53
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,480
I'm sorry. I got a little lost.

54
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,200
Danthai, come here quickly.

55
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:45,720
It's not 4 p.m. yet.
We can still sign up, right?

56
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,000
Go ahead.

57
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,360
These guys are your bandmates?

58
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,160
Can they even play instruments?

59
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,600
Of course they can.

60
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,480
Why else would we be signing up?

61
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,000
Right, guys?

62
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,520
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

63
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,880
I'm so good at it.

64
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:25,960
I can only play the melodica.

65
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,520
I've only played drums at Sports Day.

66
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,760
I've only played the <i>tingnong</i>.

67
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,000
Shit.

68
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,920
If I'd known from the start,
I wouldn't have entered.

69
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,560
Hey, come on. Give it a try.

70
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:40,840
We have five days before the first round.

71
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:45,920
We have to make it
into the final five bands.

72
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,520
- We can do it!
- We can do it!

73
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,120
My dream!

74
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:07,520
No way!

75
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,000
I'll take this one.

76
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,880
Sure. This model is really good.

77
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,120
I highly recommend it.

78
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,920
- I'll get it ready for you.
- Here.

79
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,080
How would you like to pay?

80
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,360
Here you are. My credit card.

81
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,040
Sure. Please wait a moment.

82
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,720
You're like a dog with a new toy.

83
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:49,120
Are you going to sleep
hugging that guitar tonight?

84
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,080
No.

85
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,440
I'd rather hug you.

86
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,800
You look cool when you hold a guitar.

87
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,440
Sir, I'm sorry.

88
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,520
Would another payment method work for you?

89
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,640
Your credit card was declined.

90
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,320
I'm really sorry.

91
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:15,120
Maybe next time, then.

92
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,960
We'll come back later.

93
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,360
I'm really sorry.

94
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:31,240
Hello? I'm trying to buy something,
but my credit card isn't working.

95
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:32,400
Is something wrong?

96
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,080
<i>Krit, your dad</i>
<i>had your credit card canceled.</i>

97
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:40,320
<i>He said it'll stay that way</i>
<i>until you learn what's right and wrong.</i>

98
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:42,040
<i>Do you have enough money, dear?</i>

99
00:07:42,120 --> 00:07:45,240
It's okay. I'll manage. Don't worry, Mom.

100
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,000
What happened?

101
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,240
I don't think I want to compete anymore.

102
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,920
What? Why?

103
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,040
I don't want to do this anymore.

104
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,360
I think I should stop.

105
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,000
Do you think you can teach them
to get better in time?

106
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:33,120
- No.
- Huh?

107
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,240
Your friends might not improve overnight,

108
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:40,320
but our band members never back down.

109
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,960
No wonder they're your friends.

110
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:43,880
They're your friends too.

111
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,680
You're our friend.

112
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,320
Whenever you do something you love,

113
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:55,280
no matter how hard it is,
you always give it your all.

114
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:57,920
What's with you?

115
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,280
Why are you suddenly giving me
a confidence booster?

116
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:03,280
Come on. Help me pick a song.

117
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,440
What are the options?

118
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,400
Is this one good?

119
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,040
It's not bad,
but do you have anything else?

120
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,240
Wait a second.

121
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:33,040
I've listened to this one before.

122
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,880
- This one?
- Yeah.

123
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,240
How about this one?

124
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,440
Wait.

125
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,400
Try this one.

126
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:42,920
Okay.

127
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:51,640
<i>Only you can stop my heart right here</i>

128
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:56,280
<i>Where you are</i>

129
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:02,040
<i>You're the only one I want</i>

130
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:07,560
<i>With all my soul and heart</i>

131
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:10,600
<i>I'll find every way to love you</i>

132
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:14,280
<i>No matter when or where</i>

133
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:19,440
<i>My whole heart belongs to you alone</i>

134
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,640
<i>Why did you bring me here again?</i>

135
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,000
I told you I was done.

136
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,120
Mochi.

137
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:41,200
You…

138
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,720
I'm not giving it to you for free.

139
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,440
Win the prize money, then pay me back.

140
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,400
Can I really do this?

141
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,960
Even my family doesn't believe in me.

142
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,480
Then look over there.

143
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,600
<i>I'm waiting to see you on stage, Krit!</i>

144
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,720
<i>Fighting, Krit.</i>

145
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:17,480
<i>I'm waiting for your performance.</i>

146
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,840
Even if your family doesn't support you,

147
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,920
you've gotten yourself this far.

148
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:31,000
Look.

149
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,960
So many fans are here to support you.

150
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:38,000
And you've got me cheering you on.

151
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,480
Are you really not going to keep fighting?

152
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,560
Show your dad how good you are.

153
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:07,000
I'm sorry, bro.

154
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:10,000
The professor let us out a little late.
Are we still doing this?

155
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:19,800
Come on. Let's win this!

156
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:22,720
The Winner!

157
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,640
Guys, look.

158
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:15,280
The competition hasn't even started,
yet they've already won over all the fans.

159
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:19,240
Seriously.
Their teamwork is insanely good.

160
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,760
Wow, Krit is amazing.

161
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,080
Dan!

162
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,160
Go!

163
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:27,960
I'm sorry.

164
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,680
I thought someone like me,
who only played drums on Sports Day,

165
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:34,320
could never compete with them.

166
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:46,600
I just thought of something.

167
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,880
I want to try something.

168
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:54,880
You guys brought your things, right?

169
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,880
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

170
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:11,360
Are these lucky team shirts
really going to work?

171
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,920
I don't know,

172
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,280
but we have to try everything now.

173
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,680
GOOD LUCK

174
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,960
Try it on.

175
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,320
Here.

176
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:38,040
Well? Do I look handsome?

177
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:40,920
Oh, you look handsome. Super handsome.

178
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,280
No one can compare to you.
I've never seen anyone so handsome.

179
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:45,600
You look like you've never done
anything wrong in your life.

180
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:48,480
You're exaggerating. Go put yours on too.

181
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,880
- Here.
- Hold this for me.

182
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:10,240
Oh, whoa!

183
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,200
VICTORY

184
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:14,720
"Good luck," "Victory," "nine-nine."

185
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:20,600
All these auspicious words will definitely
bring our team good fortune.

186
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,600
We'll easily pass the first round.

187
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:26,560
My boyfriend really knows
how to fill me with positivity.

188
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:30,120
Huh? Boyfriend? Nonsense.

189
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,880
Focus on the competition.

190
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:34,600
If I win, will you be my boyfriend?

191
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:43,720
You're so obsessed with this, huh?
Get through the first round first.

192
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,120
Move.

193
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:06,120
<i>Because someone unnecessary</i>
<i>Has to walk away</i>

194
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:10,720
<i>No matter how much I love you inside</i>

195
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:15,080
<i>Someone unnecessary shouldn't be here</i>

196
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:20,200
<i>I understand that you don't need me</i>

197
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:26,720
<i>I'll leave in tears as someone worthless</i>

198
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:32,080
<i>Because it's a necessity</i>
<i>Of someone unnecessary</i>

199
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:46,240
<i>Because it's a necessity</i>
<i>Of someone unnecessary</i>

200
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:54,520
This is the Winner!

201
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,240
Let's give them another round of applause!

202
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:03,040
And here are the band manager and members.

203
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:05,280
Damn. He's so good.

204
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:06,760
That's so cool.

205
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,560
We can also do it.

206
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,359
We can do it.

207
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:16,640
And our next band, please welcome Horizon!

208
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:23,760
You have 15 minutes to prepare.

209
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:26,599
Please come onstage and get ready.

210
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,480
We can do this, guys!

211
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:43,400
We can!

212
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,640
- Horizon, fight!
- Fight!

213
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,920
This will really work, right?

214
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,280
Good question.

215
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:45,520
<i>You are everything</i>
<i>In my reality and dreams</i>

216
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:50,200
<i>You are everything</i>
<i>My heart could ever want</i>

217
00:18:50,280 --> 00:18:57,200
<i>You are the story I read</i>
<i>Before I close my eyes and dream</i>

218
00:18:57,840 --> 00:19:02,280
<i>Don't tell me you're making us play</i>
<i>these main instruments too.</i>

219
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:03,400
Yeah.

220
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:06,400
Since we're doing a cover anyway,

221
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:10,000
we just have to put
our own identity into the song.

222
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,680
<i>Friends don't abandon each other.</i>

223
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:15,560
<i>Come on, Rin, Khobfa.</i>

224
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,080
Let's chase our dreams.

225
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:23,360
<i>Our band members never give up.</i>

226
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:25,280
<i>No wonder they're your friends.</i>

227
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,160
<i>They're your friends too.</i>

228
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,800
You're our friend.

229
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:34,440
<i>Right where you are</i>

230
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:40,680
<i>You're the only one I want</i>

231
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:45,160
<i>With all my soul and heart</i>

232
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:50,960
<i>I'll find every way to love you</i>
<i>No matter when or where</i>

233
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:56,400
<i>My whole heart belongs to you alone</i>

234
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:19,440
Next, we will announce the bands
selected for the finals

235
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:22,520
of the Campus Stage competition.

236
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:26,160
Only five bands
will advance to the final round.

237
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:30,160
The first selected band is…

238
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:36,520
The Winner!

239
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:48,040
Moving on to the next band…

240
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:51,960
The next band is…

241
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:55,440
Stand Still!

242
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:57,080
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

243
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:05,520
And the next band is…

244
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:07,480
Friends with Deadlines!

245
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:14,520
There are only two spots left.

246
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,160
The next band advancing is…

247
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,120
- Sakit!
- Yeah!

248
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:30,200
And now, for the final band.

249
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:34,840
This band received points
for their creativity.

250
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:40,960
Although their performance wasn't perfect,
the judges saw their determination.

251
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:46,400
The final band advancing
to the next round is…

252
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:57,400
Horizon!

253
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,120
We made it!

254
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,920
- Let's go!
- Come on!

255
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:05,600
Congratulations!

256
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:09,400
I told you my shirts work, didn't I?

257
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,800
They say "Good luck" and "Victory."

258
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,320
So we got "Lucky."

259
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,520
Lucky. Why?

260
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:18,520
Yeah.

261
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:31,040
Congratulations again
to all five bands advancing.

262
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:38,480
Over the next two weeks,

263
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:42,840
you must prepare a song
for the championship round.

264
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:45,400
Guys, we only have two weeks?

265
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:47,880
We can do it.

266
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:52,520
The rule is that every band
must perform one song.

267
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,640
You may rearrange an existing song
or write an original song.

268
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:01,840
However, bands that write an original song

269
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:07,560
will receive bonus points
from our judges for originality.

270
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:09,120
Bonus points?

271
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:13,400
Which option will each band choose?

272
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,160
Please decide by today.

273
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:18,440
You have ten minutes to discuss.

274
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,200
You may begin.

275
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,080
Writing a new song sounds interesting,

276
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:28,640
but two weeks is too little time.

277
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,360
We'd have to write the lyrics and melody,

278
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:35,240
then practice until we can play it well.

279
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:36,720
I think it's too risky.

280
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:37,720
True.

281
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:39,480
I agree.

282
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:43,000
If the new song turns out badly,
our total score will plummet.

283
00:23:43,080 --> 00:23:46,400
Let's take a song people already know
and make it cool in our own style.

284
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:48,640
- It'd be safer.
- Yeah.

285
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,840
I agree.

286
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:53,960
Khobfa, let's write a new song.

287
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:55,520
There will be bonus points.

288
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,640
Look at our band members.

289
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,600
It won't be easy, Rin.

290
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,520
Should we really play it safe?

291
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:05,680
Look at that band.

292
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:07,440
They're scary as hell.

293
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:13,960
What do you think, Khobfa?

294
00:24:14,960 --> 00:24:16,240
It's up to you.

295
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:18,040
Whatever you say, I'm in.

296
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,520
Time's up.

297
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:27,080
Please turn around.

298
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:33,920
Which bands will rearrange
an existing song?

299
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:36,680
Please have one representative
raise their hand.

300
00:24:47,080 --> 00:24:51,120
What about Horizon?

301
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:04,400
Horizon will write an original song.

302
00:25:14,360 --> 00:25:16,600
Statistically, no band has ever won

303
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:19,160
with an original song
in the past four years.

304
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:21,280
Isn't Khobfa taking too big a risk?

305
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,760
Mark Zuckerberg once said,

306
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:40,240
"The biggest risk is not taking one."

307
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:43,200
If we keep doing the same thing,

308
00:25:43,280 --> 00:25:45,200
our chances of winning are slim.

309
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:48,600
But if we take the risk,
we still have a chance.

310
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:49,920
Let's go for it.

311
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:52,480
We have nothing to lose.

312
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:55,520
You're right. Let's do this.

313
00:25:56,120 --> 00:26:00,640
Khobfa, since you said all that,
do you already have an idea?

314
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,160
- Not yet.
- What?

315
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:07,920
That's why I called you guys
to brainstorm.

316
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,560
But I have one thing in mind.

317
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:12,160
It has to be about love.

318
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:13,560
- Love?
- Love?

319
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,840
That's way too broad, man.

320
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:18,480
Can you narrow it down?

321
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:24,480
Hey, what if it's about memories of love?

322
00:26:24,560 --> 00:26:26,440
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

323
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:27,880
That sounds interesting.

324
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:28,960
How about this?

325
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:32,240
We'll take turns
sharing our memories of love,

326
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:35,160
then vote on which one is best.

327
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:36,720
- Sounds good?
- Yeah.

328
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:37,840
Okay.

329
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,920
Who wants to start?

330
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,760
Me. I'll go first.

331
00:26:46,320 --> 00:26:49,720
I've had a crush on someone
for a long time.

332
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,560
I talk to him every day,

333
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,320
but what should I do?

334
00:26:55,240 --> 00:26:56,760
It seems like he likes me,

335
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:58,840
but he won't make it clear.

336
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:00,560
Sorry, Jinnie.

337
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:02,240
You have someone you're talking to?

338
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:05,560
Come on. It's Baron.

339
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:08,800
He's AI.

340
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:10,320
- What?
- What?

341
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:13,520
I talk to him day and night.

342
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:18,680
How do I get him
to be my boyfriend already?

343
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:21,920
Oh, Jinnie. That's enough.

344
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:23,160
Sit down.

345
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:24,640
Let's hear my story instead.

346
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,960
Fluke and I.

347
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:32,880
My love story with Fluke.

348
00:27:34,040 --> 00:27:35,160
What faculty is he in?

349
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:37,120
How could I not know about this one?

350
00:27:37,720 --> 00:27:39,120
I don't know either.

351
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:42,200
We met through DMs.

352
00:27:42,280 --> 00:27:45,200
He messaged me first,
so we exchanged numbers.

353
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:49,080
He called me day and night.

354
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:53,720
But whenever he had a problem,
I had to send him money to help.

355
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:55,960
For phone credit and rent.

356
00:27:56,040 --> 00:28:00,480
There were a lot of problems later on,
so my bank account ran dry.

357
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:01,760
You idiot.

358
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:03,240
Hey.

359
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:05,440
That's called a scammer.

360
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:07,760
- A scammer?
- How did you fall for that?

361
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:09,960
You fell for an AI!

362
00:28:10,040 --> 00:28:13,880
Enough, you two. Sit down.

363
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:23,200
Dan, you're our last hope.

364
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:25,240
I hope your story is useful.

365
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,800
It should be.

366
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:30,800
But it's a little painful.

367
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:32,400
- What?
- Oh, hey.

368
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:36,760
Damn. This sounds promising.

369
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,040
I fell in love with a rice shop vendor.

370
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:41,440
- What?
- What?

371
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:46,560
Why? Love these days has no definition.

372
00:28:47,160 --> 00:28:48,480
Hold on, Dan.

373
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:50,720
How did you fall for her?

374
00:28:51,680 --> 00:28:53,920
She called me handsome.

375
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:58,600
Every time I went to her shop,
she would call me handsome.

376
00:28:58,680 --> 00:29:00,880
She even asked me to order an extra size.

377
00:29:00,960 --> 00:29:04,200
Then one day, I found out the truth.

378
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:07,600
What?

379
00:29:09,040 --> 00:29:12,400
She calls every man
who comes in "handsome."

380
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,640
Damn.

381
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:18,160
You can't play
with someone's heart like that.

382
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:25,000
Dan, there are plenty
of rice shop vendors out there.

383
00:29:25,080 --> 00:29:25,960
Okay?

384
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:30,200
Danthai, don't cry.

385
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,400
You'll make me cry too.

386
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:40,400
No, hold the ends.

387
00:29:40,480 --> 00:29:41,760
Hold the ends.

388
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,840
What's the problem?

389
00:29:43,920 --> 00:29:46,680
The strings are thick. My fingers hurt.

390
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:48,920
Press harder. Press.

391
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,040
Let me see.

392
00:29:50,120 --> 00:29:52,120
You already have some experience, right?

393
00:29:57,800 --> 00:29:58,640
I see.

394
00:29:58,720 --> 00:29:59,680
Keep practicing.

395
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:01,000
You're actually not bad.

396
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:22,280
If we hadn't talked to them,

397
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:25,360
we would never have known
they had such strange love stories.

398
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:29,040
Are they strange?

399
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:32,200
I still think they're love stories.

400
00:30:33,120 --> 00:30:37,400
Do you have a love story
you want to share with me?

401
00:30:39,320 --> 00:30:43,920
It's probably the time
I got to spend with you.

402
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:48,440
Khobfa.

403
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:53,320
If you knew I was the one
who's been making you unlucky,

404
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:55,360
would you still love me?

405
00:30:58,200 --> 00:30:59,320
<i>Why did you hide it from me?</i>

406
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:01,920
<i>A presto amora!</i>

407
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,720
<i>If you choose to inherit it,</i>
<i>you must prepare to be unlucky in love.</i>

408
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:09,360
<i>- Khobfa!</i>
- I regret ever trusting you.

409
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,640
Rin?

410
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:11,800
Rin.

411
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:15,840
What's with you?
You've been thinking for so long.

412
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:19,120
Do you have anything to share?

413
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:24,720
It's probably the time
I got to spend with you.

414
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:28,880
Same here.

415
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:34,040
You made my time so meaningful.

416
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:43,720
You're always in my business,
and you're a drunk too.

417
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:46,040
I have to get you a ride home every day.

418
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:48,680
Wait. Are you insulting me?

419
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:49,920
No.

420
00:31:55,640 --> 00:31:59,400
Honestly, you've always supported me.

421
00:31:59,480 --> 00:32:01,200
Without you,

422
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:04,720
I never thought I could come this far.

423
00:32:06,880 --> 00:32:10,720
Thank you, really,
for coming into my life.

424
00:32:33,560 --> 00:32:34,880
Rin.

425
00:32:36,040 --> 00:32:38,600
I left the report
due this evening in my room.

426
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:42,120
Can you get it for me?
I haven't finished practicing yet.

427
00:32:42,200 --> 00:32:45,840
Okay. You keep practicing. I'll get it.

428
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:47,440
It's your old room.

429
00:32:47,520 --> 00:32:49,400
I already claimed it from you.

430
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,440
Yeah.

431
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:52,320
Wait.

432
00:32:52,400 --> 00:32:54,880
Hasn't the owner asked for the house back?

433
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:02,000
Dan's mom owns the house.

434
00:33:02,080 --> 00:33:03,960
She is the owner.

435
00:33:04,040 --> 00:33:07,200
- Right, Dan?
- Yeah. She's renovating it to sell.

436
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:10,600
I'm off.

437
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:16,320
I'll get back to practicing, then.

438
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,920
Damn. My room!

439
00:33:33,760 --> 00:33:36,480
Gosh. It's such a mess.

440
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,760
Where is it?

441
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,600
Dan didn't tell me.

442
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:09,440
Oh shit! This is the missing page
from the owl spellbook.

443
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:26,000
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE
ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER

444
00:34:26,719 --> 00:34:30,560
Why is the cure for the curse here?

445
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:42,520
<i>To lift the curse,</i>

446
00:34:42,600 --> 00:34:47,719
<i>the curser must take the item used for it,</i>
<i>make a wish, and recite</i>

447
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:50,040
"finito amora."

448
00:34:50,120 --> 00:34:53,199
<i>However, once the curse is lifted,</i>

449
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:57,280
<i>the cursed person will lose</i>
<i>all memories of the curser,</i>

450
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:59,480
<i>as if they never knew each other.</i>

451
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:06,240
"The cursed person will lose
all memories of the curser."

452
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:23,440
<i>I found a way to lift the curse, guys.</i>

453
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:28,000
<i>Congratulations, Rin.</i>

454
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:29,400
<i>Do it quickly.</i>

455
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:31,720
<i>The spirits have opened the way.</i>

456
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:37,000
<i>If you don't do it now,</i>
<i>something worse might happen.</i>

457
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:49,400
THE CURSER MUST TAKE THE ITEM USED FOR IT,
MAKE A WISH, AND RECITE "<i>FINITO AMORA</i>."

458
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:50,800
HOWEVER, ONCE THE CURSE IS LIFTED,

459
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:52,600
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE
ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER

460
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:10,800
<i>Yet there is one lucky thing.</i>

461
00:36:11,640 --> 00:36:14,360
<i>Whatever happens, you are always there.</i>

462
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:17,640
<i>Your birthday is on the final day.</i>

463
00:36:18,240 --> 00:36:21,000
<i>I want us to share a memory that day.</i>

464
00:36:50,400 --> 00:36:51,360
Hey.

465
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:56,240
Congratulations on
passing the first round.

466
00:36:56,320 --> 00:36:59,080
Thanks. You too.

467
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:02,320
I liked your guitar sound
in the last round.

468
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:05,840
Me too. I liked your rearrangement.

469
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:09,680
I'm going all out in the final round.

470
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:12,800
Same here.
There's no way I'll lose to you.

471
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:29,280
I MIGHT BE UNLUCKY

472
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:43,360
You've been working hard
since early morning.

473
00:37:46,880 --> 00:37:50,000
I want to finish writing the song
so we have time to practice with our band.

474
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:53,800
Don't you have an exam today?

475
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:55,040
I bought you congee.

476
00:37:55,120 --> 00:37:56,880
Eat quickly, then go take your exam.

477
00:37:57,560 --> 00:38:00,280
Thanks. Have you eaten?

478
00:38:00,360 --> 00:38:02,560
Take a break and eat congee with me, okay?

479
00:38:03,440 --> 00:38:04,760
I'll get it ready.

480
00:38:06,760 --> 00:38:10,440
Hey, are you okay?

481
00:38:11,040 --> 00:38:13,360
You're burning up.

482
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:14,480
Hey.

483
00:38:16,920 --> 00:38:18,400
You should get some rest.

484
00:39:10,600 --> 00:39:11,600
I'm full.

485
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:14,680
Then…

486
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,600
Take some medicine.

487
00:39:18,680 --> 00:39:20,200
No.

488
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:22,080
I said take it.

489
00:39:22,680 --> 00:39:23,800
No.

490
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:26,520
You have to. Here.

491
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:43,200
All right. Now go get some sleep.

492
00:39:45,520 --> 00:39:47,600
But I haven't finished the song.

493
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:52,000
Hey, rest first.

494
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:54,600
Sleep. Trust me.

495
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:20,800
<i>Once the curse is lifted,</i>

496
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:25,120
<i>the cursed person will lose</i>
<i>all memories of the curser,</i>

497
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:27,480
<i>as if they never knew each other.</i>

498
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:41,240
Did Khobfa forget to water you?

499
00:40:41,800 --> 00:40:43,800
You're wilting just like your owner.

500
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:52,480
Sorry, but he's focused
on his band right now.

501
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,560
Hello? What's up?

502
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:02,680
<i>Rin, where are you?</i>

503
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:05,360
<i>There's a graded body-painting exam today.</i>

504
00:41:05,440 --> 00:41:07,760
<i>The professor</i>
<i>called your name three times.</i>

505
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:08,800
<i>Did you forget?</i>

506
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:10,520
I didn't forget.

507
00:41:10,600 --> 00:41:11,960
I probably can't make it.

508
00:41:12,040 --> 00:41:14,960
Khobfa is sick,
so I have to stay with him.

509
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:16,680
Go take your exam.

510
00:41:18,200 --> 00:41:19,360
I'm fine.

511
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:21,920
I don't want you to fail an exam
because of me.

512
00:41:24,480 --> 00:41:28,520
Ohm, I'm taking leave today.
Please tell the professor. Bye.

513
00:41:30,160 --> 00:41:32,680
You're usually serious
about grades, right?

514
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:37,840
But you're the most important thing
right now.

515
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:49,960
I've decided. It's okay.

516
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,960
Go back to sleep.

517
00:41:57,520 --> 00:41:58,840
I'll give you five minutes.

518
00:42:01,600 --> 00:42:02,600
For what?

519
00:42:06,720 --> 00:42:08,960
I'm sorry.
I was talking to a customer for so long.

520
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:10,200
Come on. Let's eat.

521
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:12,880
What are you doing?

522
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:16,520
Wait. Turn around first.

523
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:18,600
Yeah, turn around.

524
00:42:21,560 --> 00:42:22,560
What are you doing?

525
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:24,240
Just a second.

526
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:30,600
Turn around.

527
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:33,960
Surprise!

528
00:42:34,040 --> 00:42:35,280
What do you think?

529
00:42:35,880 --> 00:42:37,480
I made this for you.

530
00:42:37,560 --> 00:42:38,920
Wow.

531
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:40,520
Come sit down.

532
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:43,200
Hurry.

533
00:42:46,640 --> 00:42:51,360
I may not have much money,
but this is what I can do right now.

534
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:55,640
When I win the prize money,

535
00:42:56,760 --> 00:42:58,800
I'll treat you to a special meal.

536
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:01,920
This is already very special.

537
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:04,680
What?

538
00:43:05,320 --> 00:43:06,960
Nothing. Let me taste it.

539
00:43:07,040 --> 00:43:09,320
Wait.

540
00:43:10,920 --> 00:43:12,200
I'll feed you.

541
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:15,920
Open wide.

542
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:24,640
How is it? Is it okay?

543
00:43:33,040 --> 00:43:34,160
Better than I expected.

544
00:43:34,240 --> 00:43:35,160
Are you lying?

545
00:43:35,240 --> 00:43:36,520
No, really. Taste it.

546
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:55,840
Khobfa, enough.

547
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:57,840
My professor is strict.
He won't listen to you.

548
00:43:57,920 --> 00:44:01,160
No. I caused you trouble,
so I have to take responsibility.

549
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:02,960
No need.

550
00:44:04,240 --> 00:44:05,400
I'll handle it.

551
00:44:12,440 --> 00:44:13,720
Hello, Professor.

552
00:44:13,800 --> 00:44:15,200
Hello, Professor.

553
00:44:15,720 --> 00:44:19,160
I'm really sorry Rin missed the exam.

554
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:20,280
It was because of me.

555
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:22,480
He had to stay and take care of me.

556
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:24,280
Please don't deduct Rin's grades.

557
00:44:26,880 --> 00:44:28,280
Rules are rules.

558
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:30,040
You missed the body-painting exam.

559
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:33,800
It's worth 30 points, Rin. Understand?

560
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:34,840
Yes, Professor.

561
00:44:34,920 --> 00:44:36,160
But the time isn't up yet, right?

562
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:39,920
The other students
just finished early, correct?

563
00:44:40,640 --> 00:44:45,280
I'm sorry. I called Ohm and Jinnie.

564
00:44:46,640 --> 00:44:50,400
You're right. You have 90 minutes left.

565
00:44:50,480 --> 00:44:52,200
Can you finish in time, Rin?

566
00:44:52,800 --> 00:44:54,600
- Ninety minutes, Professor?
- Yes.

567
00:44:55,920 --> 00:44:57,880
Where am I going to find a model?

568
00:44:57,960 --> 00:44:59,480
I already gave up my booking.

569
00:45:06,360 --> 00:45:10,400
I'm sorry. Am I the only one
who doesn't know what's going on?

570
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:17,160
Come here.

571
00:45:36,840 --> 00:45:39,640
Easy. Take it slow.

572
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:41,720
Don't worry.

573
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:43,640
Idiot!

574
00:45:45,880 --> 00:45:46,800
You can do it.

575
00:46:44,320 --> 00:46:49,480
<i>I might be unlucky</i>

576
00:46:50,080 --> 00:46:54,880
<i>As if I'm cursed with bad luck</i>

577
00:46:56,200 --> 00:46:57,200
Hey!

578
00:46:58,160 --> 00:47:00,560
I just thought of the melody
for our new song.

579
00:47:00,640 --> 00:47:02,080
Keep painting.

580
00:47:05,600 --> 00:47:10,480
<i>I might be unlucky</i>

581
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:16,800
<i>As if I'm cursed with bad luck</i>

582
00:47:18,040 --> 00:47:21,200
<i>Whatever I do, I end up hurt</i>

583
00:47:21,800 --> 00:47:25,280
<i>Disappointed in everything</i>

584
00:47:26,320 --> 00:47:30,560
<i>Yet there is one lucky thing</i>

585
00:47:31,080 --> 00:47:35,640
<i>Whatever happens, you are always there</i>

586
00:47:36,320 --> 00:47:40,040
<i>No matter how unlucky I am</i>

587
00:47:40,120 --> 00:47:42,960
<i>I'm lucky</i>

588
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:48,640
<i>Just to have you in my life</i>

589
00:47:53,320 --> 00:47:55,720
How is it? Do you like it?

590
00:47:58,040 --> 00:47:59,040
Yeah.

591
00:48:00,440 --> 00:48:02,040
I love it.

592
00:48:02,120 --> 00:48:05,040
I secretly put our story
into the song too.

593
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:09,840
<i>Yet there is one lucky thing</i>

594
00:48:09,920 --> 00:48:14,000
<i>Whatever happens, you are always there</i>

595
00:48:14,080 --> 00:48:16,600
<i>No matter how unlucky I am</i>

596
00:48:16,680 --> 00:48:20,120
<i>I'm lucky</i>

597
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:25,520
<i>Just to have you in my life</i>

598
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,800
I wouldn't call this decent.

599
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:46,720
It's outstanding. An A for sure.

600
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:48,160
A D wouldn't do it justice.

601
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:52,080
- Thank you, Professor.
- Thank you.

602
00:48:53,360 --> 00:48:56,360
Pack up, clean yourself up, and go home.

603
00:48:56,440 --> 00:48:57,320
- Yes.
- Okay.

604
00:48:59,200 --> 00:49:02,960
Damn. It's A-level work.

605
00:49:03,040 --> 00:49:04,240
Let me take some photos.

606
00:49:04,320 --> 00:49:05,160
Come on.

607
00:49:05,880 --> 00:49:08,520
Whoa, look.

608
00:49:09,200 --> 00:49:10,920
I don't think you need to shower tonight.

609
00:49:11,520 --> 00:49:12,640
Great job.

610
00:49:22,200 --> 00:49:23,560
What should we do?

611
00:49:23,640 --> 00:49:25,040
It won't wash off.

612
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:31,160
Just leave it. It's fine.

613
00:49:31,240 --> 00:49:34,840
But if you leave it, you'll stay stained.

614
00:49:34,920 --> 00:49:36,040
Is that okay?

615
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:38,520
It's fine.

616
00:49:38,600 --> 00:49:43,160
It'll be a trace of our good memories.
Isn't that nice?

617
00:49:51,080 --> 00:49:52,400
Is this spot done yet?

618
00:50:11,360 --> 00:50:12,760
Can I kiss you?

619
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:14,840
What?

620
00:50:14,920 --> 00:50:17,280
Are you going to kiss me
to prove true love again?

621
00:50:17,360 --> 00:50:18,920
This isn't Rayong.

622
00:50:19,520 --> 00:50:21,760
Please. Just once.

623
00:50:21,840 --> 00:50:22,720
Please.

624
00:50:24,920 --> 00:50:26,440
But…

625
00:50:26,520 --> 00:50:29,200
Think of it as my reward
for talking to the professor for you.

626
00:50:29,280 --> 00:50:32,560
Wow, now you're holding that over me.

627
00:50:33,640 --> 00:50:35,600
So? Will you allow me to?

628
00:50:35,680 --> 00:50:37,960
If you take too long, I'll take two.

629
00:50:41,440 --> 00:50:42,840
Fine.

630
00:52:07,720 --> 00:52:09,400
Would it be too selfish of me?

631
00:52:13,520 --> 00:52:15,920
THE CURSED PERSON WILL LOSE
ALL MEMORIES OF THE CURSER,

632
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:17,640
AS IF THEY NEVER KNEW EACH OTHER.

633
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:21,320
Rin, I'm done.

634
00:52:28,840 --> 00:52:30,760
Come on. Let's go back to the room.

635
00:52:40,160 --> 00:52:41,280
I'll tie it for you.

636
00:52:45,840 --> 00:52:47,760
<i>I'm sorry, Khobfa.</i>

637
00:52:48,720 --> 00:52:50,280
<i>I just want to…</i>

638
00:52:51,920 --> 00:52:54,000
<i>stay in your memories a little longer.</i>

639
00:53:12,280 --> 00:53:13,640
<i>Our band is getting in sync.</i>

640
00:53:13,720 --> 00:53:16,600
<i>If this keeps up,</i>
<i>we'll do great in the final round.</i>

641
00:53:16,680 --> 00:53:19,200
<i>Thank you for always believing in me.</i>

642
00:53:19,280 --> 00:53:20,760
During the final rehearsal and the final,

643
00:53:20,840 --> 00:53:23,000
I'm going to surprise Rin
and ask him to be my boyfriend.

644
00:53:23,080 --> 00:53:25,200
<i>What? You're going to ask Rin out?</i>

645
00:53:25,280 --> 00:53:26,600
<i>Just open your heart.</i>

646
00:53:27,200 --> 00:53:28,320
<i>I'm waiting for you.</i>

647
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:30,520
<i>Or should I lift the curse?</i>

648
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:33,720
<i>But if you don't,</i>
<i>Khobfa will be unlucky forever.</i>

649
00:53:34,320 --> 00:53:37,280
Would you take someone unlucky
as your boyfriend?

650
00:53:37,360 --> 00:53:40,040
- Date him!
- Date him!

651
00:53:40,120 --> 00:53:42,200
BE MY BOYFRIEND
